An issue with the previous implementation was that `OpportunityContactRole` records (and existing `npsp__Partial_Soft_Credit__c` records) were queried with read-only fields like `OpportunityId` and `ContactId` and then passed directly to `update`/`upsert`. When DML is checked for field accessibility or run under user-mode enforcement, Salesforce rejects updates on SObjects that contain read-only fields.

By constructing fresh SObjects for update containing only `Id` and writeable fields (`Role` on `OpportunityContactRole`, and `Amount`/`Role_Name`/`Contact_Role_ID` on `npsp__Partial_Soft_Credit__c`), inaccessible field exceptions are avoided.

